# Local Orchestrator

Use the local Ollama + SQLite RAG **orchestrator** (not Cursor Cloud) to fan out to specialist agents and aggregate findings:

```bash
./scripts/pr-review-index.sh   # shared RAG index
./scripts/orchestrate.sh       # pr + security + performance
./scripts/orchestrate.sh --pr 42
./scripts/orchestrate.sh --parallel
./scripts/orchestrate.sh --bug "..." --pr 42
```

Rules: `agents/orchestrator/RULES.md`.
Index: `agents/pr-reviewer/index/rag.sqlite` (shared).

Default specialists:

- `pr` — architecture / BLoC / contracts (`./scripts/pr-review.sh`)
- `security` — secrets, TLS, storage, logging (`./scripts/sec-review.sh`)
- `performance` — rebuild / scroll / isolate jank (`./scripts/perf-review.sh`)
- `bug` — only with `--bug` / `--stacktrace` or `--agents bug`

Prefer the orchestrator when the user wants a full local review pass. Keep findings actionable and agent-tagged. Never auto-patch or merge.
